    <figure xml:id="fig-fast-mode">
      <caption>
        The fast mode, drawn to the same scale as
        <xref ref="fig-slow-mode" text="type-global"/>: the motion that starts along
        <m>\vec{x}_2 = (1,-1)</m>. The carts are always displaced by <m>u</m> in
        <em>opposite</em> directions, so the middle spring is squeezed and stretched by
        <m>2u</m><mdash/>twice what either cart moves<mdash/>while both outer springs
        act together. Every spring now pulls back on every cart, the restoring force is
        stronger than in the slow mode, and the carts vibrate faster: this extra
        stiffness is the larger eigenvalue <m>3</m>, giving
        <m>\omega_2 = \sqrt{3}\,\omega_1</m>.
      </caption>
